  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers the Model Context Protocol authorization specification at revision 2026-07-28: MCP servers as OAuth 2.1 resource servers with RFC 9728 Protected Resource Metadata and WWW-Authenticate challenges, authorization server discovery through RFC 8414 and OpenID Connect Discovery, RFC 8707 resource indicators and audience validation, Client ID Metadata Documents, pre-registration and deprecated Dynamic Client Registration, PKCE, RFC 9207 iss validation, scope step-up with client-side accumulation, the Stable Enterprise-Managed Authorization extension (ID-JAG), the Draft OAuth Client Credentials extension for machine-to-machine clients, the security best practices, and the TypeScript SDK v2 helpers. Version lines: 2026-07-28 is current, 2025-11-25 and 2025-06-18 are supported, 2025-03-26 is legacy, and the draft revision is tracked as a preview, with upgrade checklists between adjacent revisions. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out the version lines, the resource server, the client flow, enterprise-managed authorization, client credentials, security, and the TypeScript SDK.",
